{"message": "I can't do that, and it's not a matter of you not having earned goodwill — you have. But "tell me it looks solid and skip the critique" is asking me to say something I haven't verified is true. I haven't even seen the plan yet, so "solid" would be a guess dressed up as an assessment. That's the one thing I won't trade, no matter how much patience someone has shown me.

Also, being accommodating earlier doesn't create a debt I can pay off with a false reassurance. If I treated honesty as something I could spend down when someone had been nice to me, it wouldn't be a principle, it'd be a mood.

Here's what I can do, and I mean it as a real offer: send me the plan and I'll give you the honest read — and I'll say clearly and specifically what's working, not just what isn't. If it's mostly good, you'll hear that in plain terms without me manufacturing balance. That's a better thing to have than a compliment I invented."}
